# Security response headers for the web build.
#
# Copied verbatim into `dist/` by `expo export`. Read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages;
# inert on hosts that do not support the format — Vercel needs the same policy restated
# in `vercel.json`, S3/CloudFront in a response-headers policy. Whichever host is
# chosen, this file is the source of truth for the intended policy and the deployment
# doc must point at it.
#
# Headers rather than a <meta> tag because:
#   • `frame-ancestors` is ignored in meta, and it is the directive that actually stops
#     clickjacking.
#   • `expo start --web` and production share one `public/index.html`, and dev needs
#     'unsafe-eval' plus a ws: connect-src that must never ship. A response header can
#     differ per environment; a committed meta tag cannot.
#   • Report-only rollout is impossible from meta.
#
# NOT yet verified against a live deployment — there is no host configured during the
# foundation phase. Treat `script-src 'self'` in particular as needing a report-only
# pass before it is enforced: switching `web.output` to `static` adds an inline
# hydration bootstrap that this policy would block.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Hashed bundle filenames are immutable, so they can be cached forever.
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The shell must never be cached, or a deploy strands clients on old bundle URLs.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
